    "Parent functions to recognize by shape and name: linear, quadratic, exponential, absolute value, square root, cube root. Only the linear parent <span class='math'>f(x) = x</span> is a straight line with a constant rate of change."],
   examples:[
    {q:"The sequence −13, −9, −5, ... continues. What is the 20th term?", src:"GaDOE Item Bank 01A2024, Part A · DOK 3",
     steps:["Find <i>d</i>: −9 − (−13) = 4. Each term adds 4.","Use the explicit formula with <i>a</i><sub>1</sub> = −13, <i>n</i> = 20: <span class='math'>a<sub>20</sub> = −13 + (20 − 1)(4)</span>.","= −13 + 76 = <b>63</b>.","General rule: <span class='math'>a<sub>n</sub> = −13 + 4(n − 1)</span>, which simplifies to <span class='math'>a<sub>n</sub> = 4n − 17</span>."]},
