 S01:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>Look at the quadratic function shown below.</p><p class="math">f(x) = x<sup>2</sup> − 8x + 15</p><p>Which equivalent form of the function reveals the minimum of the graph of the function?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","f(x) = (x − 4)<sup>2</sup> + 15","Completing the square without subtracting the added 16"],["b","f(x) = (x − 4)<sup>2</sup> − 1",""],["c","f(x) = (x − 3)(x − 5)","Factored form shows zeros, not the minimum"],["d","f(x) = (x + 3)(x + 5)","Sign error when factoring"]], ans:"b",
  why:"Vertex form shows the minimum. Complete the square: x<sup>2</sup> − 8x + 16 − 16 + 15 = (x − 4)<sup>2</sup> − 1. The minimum point is (4, −1). Choice C is equivalent but shows the zeros, not the minimum."},
 S02:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>Which function can be used to model the data in this table?</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="data"><tr><th>x</th><th>f(x)</th></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>−1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2</td></tr></table></div>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","f(x) = 3x","Ignored the starting value (y-intercept)"],["b","f(x) = x/2 − 1",""],["c","f(x) = x − 1","Used rise alone as slope (forgot to divide by run)"],["d","f(x) = 2x − 1","Inverted slope (run over rise)"]], ans:"b",
  why:"At x = 0 the output is −1, so b = −1. Slope = (0 − (−1)) / (2 − 0) = 1/2. Check x = 6: 6/2 − 1 = 2 ✓."},
 S03:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>Which statement explains why <span class="math">√5 + 4/7</span> is irrational?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","Both √5 and 4/7 are irrational. The sum of two irrational numbers is always irrational.","Thinks a fraction is irrational; overgeneralizes irrational + irrational"],["b","Both √5 and 4/7 are rational. The sum of two rational numbers is always irrational.","Thinks every square root is rational; misstates rational sum rule"],["c","√5 is irrational and 4/7 is rational. The sum of an irrational number and a rational number is always irrational.",""],["d","√5 is rational and 4/7 is irrational. The sum of a rational number and an irrational number is always irrational.","Swapped which number is rational"]], ans:"c",
