 S04:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>Look at the quadratic equation below.</p><p class="math">x<sup>2</sup> + 6x + 7 = 0</p><p>What are the solutions of the quadratic equation?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","x = −3 ± √2",""],["b","x = −6 ± √2","Did not divide −b by 2a"],["c","x = −3 ± 2√2","Divided only part of the quadratic formula by 2a"],["d","x = −6 ± 2√2","Did not divide by 2a at all"]], ans:"a",
  why:"Complete the square: x<sup>2</sup> + 6x + 9 = −7 + 9 → (x + 3)<sup>2</sup> = 2 → x + 3 = ±√2 → x = −3 ± √2. Quadratic formula check: (−6 ± √(36 − 28)) / 2 = (−6 ± 2√2)/2 = −3 ± √2."},
 S05:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>The squirrel population in a forest has grown at a constant percent rate. The table shows the number of squirrels in the forest over a 3-year period.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="data"><tr><th>Year</th><th>Number of Squirrels</th></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>1,000</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1,100</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1,210</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1,331</td></tr></table></div><p>What is the constant percent rate of change of the squirrel population?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","10%",""],["b","11%","Did not compute the ratio from one year to the next"],["c","12%","Did not compute the ratio from one year to the next"],["d","13%","Did not compute the ratio from one year to the next"]], ans:"a",
  why:"Divide each year by the year before: 1100 ÷ 1000 = 1.1, 1210 ÷ 1100 = 1.1, 1331 ÷ 1210 = 1.1. Growth factor 1.1 = 1 + 0.10, so the rate is 10%. The differences (100, 110, 121) grow, which is why this is exponential, not linear."},
 S06:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>Which scatterplot shows the strongest positive correlation coefficient?</p><div class="plots">${
    scatterFig([[2,1],[2,2],[3,3],[4,3],[4,4],[5,4],[6,6],[7,6],[7,7]],[1,.7,7.6,7.4],"a")+
