 S12:{src:"Test-style item", stem: JAM_STEM + jamFig() + `<p>Which statement is true about the cost to make a container of the strawberry jam?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","The cost to make a container of the strawberry jam was $3.10 in the year the company opened, and the cost increased $0.05 each year.",""],["b","The cost to make a container of the strawberry jam was $0.05 in the year the company opened, and the cost increased $3.10 each year.","Swapped the starting value and the rate"],["c","The cost to make a container of the strawberry jam was $3.10 in the year the company opened, and the cost increased 5 percent each year.","Read a linear rate as a percent (exponential)"],["d","The cost to make a container of the strawberry jam was $0.05 in the year the company opened, and the cost increased 3.1 percent each year.","Swapped values and treated the function as exponential"]], ans:"a",
  why:"s(x) = 3.10 + 0.05x is linear. When x = 0 (the year it opened), s(0) = 3.10. The cost adds $0.05 for each year: a constant amount, not a percent."},
 S13:{src:"Test-style item", stem: JAM_STEM + jamFig() + `<p>What does <span class="math">g(4) = 3.04</span> represent in this context?</p>`,
