 S17:{src:"Test-style item", stem:`<p>Kayla is standing on top of a cliff. She throws a rock up into the air, and the rock falls into the canyon below. She releases the rock at a height of 80 meters above the canyon. The rock follows the path of a parabola, reaching a maximum height of 100 meters 2 seconds after Kayla releases the rock, before falling into the canyon below.</p><p><b>Graph the rock's height, in meters, above the canyon x seconds after Kayla releases the rock.</b> Tap once to place the vertex, then tap a second point the parabola passes through.</p>`,
  type:"parabola",
  why:"The maximum is the vertex: (2, 100). The release point at time 0 is (0, 80). Using y = a(x − 2)<sup>2</sup> + 100 with (0, 80): 80 = 4a + 100, so a = −5. The function is y = −5(x − 2)<sup>2</sup> + 100. By symmetry it also passes through (4, 80), and it reaches the canyon floor near x ≈ 6.47 s.",
  tags:{vertex:"Vertex not at the maximum (2, 100)",point:"Parabola does not pass through the release point (0, 80)"}},

 /* ---- GaDOE Item Bank ---- */
 IB01:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 01A2024 · DOK 3", stem:`<p>Use the sequence: −13, −9, −5, ...</p><p><b>Part A.</b> If this pattern continues, what would be the 20th term in the sequence?</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["20th term",63,0.001]], tagFor:v => v===67 ? "Used n instead of (n − 1) in the explicit formula" : v===-63 ? "Sign error with the first term" : "Arithmetic sequence calculation error",
  why:"d = 4. a<sub>20</sub> = −13 + (20 − 1)(4) = −13 + 76 = 63."},
 IB03:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 03A2024 · DOK 1", stem:`<p>Sarah measures the height of her tomato plant over several weeks.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table class="data"><tr><th>Time (weeks) x</th><th>Height (cm) f(x)</th></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>15.2</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>18.4</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>21.6</td></tr></table></div><p>Which of the following equations best models the height of the plant over time?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","f(x) = 1.2x + 15.2","Slope calculation error"],["b","f(x) = 1.6x + 15.2",""],["c","f(x) = 2.1x + 14.0","Wrong slope and wrong starting value"],["d","f(x) = 1.6x + 12.0","Wrong starting value (y-intercept)"]], ans:"b",
  why:"At x = 0 the height is 15.2, so b = 15.2. Slope = (18.4 − 15.2) ÷ (2 − 0) = 3.2 ÷ 2 = 1.6 cm per week."},
 IB06:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 06A2024 · DOK 1", stem:`<p>Danielle uses C for monthly internet cost and G for gigabytes used. Select the linear function for a provider that charges $2.50 per gigabyte with a monthly fee of $20.</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","C(G) = 20G + 2.50","Swapped the rate and the starting value"],["b","C(G) = 2.50G + 20",""],["c","C(G) = 2.50 + 20G","Swapped the rate and the starting value"],["d","C(G) = 20G − 2.50","Swapped the rate and starting value; wrong operation"]], ans:"b",
  why:"The per-gigabyte cost multiplies G: 2.50G. The flat $20 fee is added once: C(G) = 2.50G + 20."},
 IB07B:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 07A2024, Part B · DOK 1", stem:`<p>A school receives $1000 in donations on the first day, and each day after, donations increase by $50. Choose the arithmetic sequence.</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["a","D(n) = 50 + 1000 · (n − 1)","Swapped the first term and the common difference"],["b","D(n) = 1000 + 50 · (n + 1)","Used (n + 1) instead of (n − 1)"],["c","D(n) = 1000 + 50 · (n − 1)",""],["d","D(n) = 50 + 1000 · (n + 1)","Swapped values and used (n + 1)"]], ans:"c",
  why:"a<sub>1</sub> = 1000 and d = 50. Explicit form a<sub>n</sub> = a<sub>1</sub> + (n − 1)d gives D(n) = 1000 + 50(n − 1). Check day 1: 1000 + 0 = 1000 ✓."},
 IB10:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 10A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>The Senior Sponsors must stay within $6000 for the senior trip. The cost is $175 per student and $150 per adult. What is the maximum number of students that can attend if 10 adults are going?</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["Maximum students",25,0.001]], tagFor:v => v===26 ? "Rounded a maximum up (breaks the budget)" : v===34 ? "Ignored the adults' cost" : v===40 ? "Divided by the adult price instead of the student price" : "Inequality setup or solving error",
  why:"175s + 150(10) ≤ 6000 → 175s + 1500 ≤ 6000 → 175s ≤ 4500 → s ≤ 25.7. You can't take part of a student, and 26 would go over budget, so the maximum is 25."},
 IB14B:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 14A2024, Part B · DOK 2", stem:`<p>The banquet hall charges $12 for adults and $8 for kids. Would the party planner be able to stay within her $600 budget for guests if 20 adults and 60 kids came?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["yes","Yes, the cost is within the budget.","Arithmetic error checking a point against a constraint"],["no","No, the cost is over the budget.",""]], ans:"no",
  why:"12(20) + 8(60) = 240 + 480 = 720. Since 720 &gt; 600, the point (20, 60) is not a solution of 12a + 8k ≤ 600. It is not possible."},
 IB16C:{src:"Built from GaDOE Item Bank 16A2024", stem:`<p>Esmerelda's family buys cinnamon rolls at $3.75 each and cookies at $1.25 each. They have $40.00 to spend and must buy at least 16 items combined. The system is <span class="math">3.75r + 1.25c ≤ 40</span> and <span class="math">r + c ≥ 16</span>.</p><p>Is buying 8 cinnamon rolls and 8 cookies a solution?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["yes","Yes. It meets both constraints.",""],["no","No. It is on the boundary line, so it doesn't count.","Thinks points on a solid (≤ or ≥) boundary are not solutions"]], ans:"yes",
  why:"3.75(8) + 1.25(8) = 30 + 10 = 40 ≤ 40 ✓ and 8 + 8 = 16 ≥ 16 ✓. The point sits exactly on both boundary lines, and both lines are solid (≤ and ≥), so it counts. They spend exactly $40."},
 IB38:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 38A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>Harry kicks a football. Its height in feet is given by <span class="math">h(t) = −16t<sup>2</sup> + 48t</span>, where t is the time in seconds after the kick. Select <b>all</b> statements that are true.</p>`,
  type:"multi", opts:[["A","The football reaches its maximum height at 1.5 seconds after the kick."],["B","The vertex of the graph represents the maximum time the football was in the air."],["C","The football was increasing in height from 1 to 2 seconds."],["D","The football was 32 feet from the ground at 1 and 2 seconds."],["E","The football lands back on the ground 3 seconds after the kick."]], ans:["A","D","E"],
  wrongTags:{A:"Could not locate the vertex",B:"Confused maximum height with maximum time",C:"Misread increasing/decreasing intervals around the vertex",D:"Did not evaluate the function at given inputs",E:"Could not find the zero (landing time)"},
  why:"Vertex at t = −48 / (2 · −16) = 1.5 s, so A is true. The vertex is the maximum <i>height</i>, not time, so B is false. Height increases from 0 to 1.5 and decreases after, so C is false. h(1) = −16 + 48 = 32 and h(2) = −64 + 96 = 32, so D is true. h(t) = −16t(t − 3) = 0 at t = 3, so E is true."},
 IB36:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 36A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>The revenue from selling x headphones is <span class="math">R(x) = −2x<sup>2</sup> + 60x</span>.</p><p>How many headphones should the company sell to maximize revenue, and what is the maximum revenue?</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["Headphones",15,0.001],["Maximum revenue ($)",450,0.01]], tagFor:()=>"Could not find or interpret the vertex (maximum)",
  why:"x = −60 / (2 · −2) = 15 headphones. R(15) = −2(225) + 60(15) = −450 + 900 = $450."},
 IB34:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 34A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>Profit from baseball necklaces is <span class="math">f(x) = −9x<sup>2</sup> + 465x − 3060</span>, where x is the selling price. Find the price that gives maximum profit. Round to the nearest cent.</p>`,
