  why:"x = −465 / (2 · −9) = 465 / 18 ≈ 25.83. Selling at about $25.83 gives the maximum profit (about $2,946.25)."},
 IB35:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 35A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>A soccer ball's height in meters is <span class="math">h(t) = −5t<sup>2</sup> + 20t + 2</span>. At what time will the ball hit the ground? Round to the nearest hundredth.</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["Time (s)",4.10,0.011]], tagFor:v => (v<0) ? "Kept the negative root (time can't be negative)" : v===2 ? "Gave the vertex time instead of the zero" : "Quadratic formula error",
  why:"Set h(t) = 0. t = (−20 ± √(400 + 40)) / (−10). The positive root is (20 + √440) / 10 ≈ (20 + 20.98) / 10 ≈ 4.10 s. The other root is negative, so reject it."},
 IB47:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 47A2024, Part A · DOK 3", stem:`<p>The function <span class="math">S(t) = 500(1.2)<sup>t</sup></span> models the number of cell phones sold t months after release. How many cell phones are sold after 3 months?</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["Phones",864,0.5]], tagFor:v => v===1800 ? "Multiplied instead of using an exponent (500 · 1.2 · 3)" : v===600 ? "Evaluated at t = 1" : "Exponential evaluation error",
  why:"S(3) = 500(1.2)<sup>3</sup> = 500(1.728) = 864."},
 IB52:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 52A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>A population of bacteria is modeled by <span class="math">P(t) = 500(1.20)<sup>t</sup></span>, where t is time in hours. Is the population increasing or decreasing over time?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["inc","Increasing, because the growth factor 1.20 is greater than 1.",""],["dec","Decreasing, because 0.20 is less than 1.","Read the rate (0.20) as the factor"]], ans:"inc",
