 IB17:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 17A2024 · DOK 2", stem:`<p>Piece B of wood is √108 feet long. Which of the following measurements would be equivalent to √108 feet? Select <b>all</b> that apply.</p>`,
  type:"multi", opts:[["1","6√3"],["2","12√3"],["3","3√12"],["4","9√3"],["5","3√9"]], ans:["1","3"],
  wrongTags:{"1":"Could not simplify √108","2":"Pulled out the wrong factor","3":"Did not recognize 3√12 = 6√3","4":"Pulled out the wrong factor","5":"Swapped the outside and inside numbers"},
  why:"√108 = √(36 · 3) = 6√3. Also 3√12 = 3 · 2√3 = 6√3. 12√3 and 9√3 are too big, and 3√9 = 9."},
 IB22:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 22A2024 · DOK 1", stem:`<p>Is √25 a rational or an irrational number?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["r","Rational",""],["i","Irrational","Thinks any square root is irrational"]], ans:"r",
  why:"25 is a perfect square, so √25 = 5 = 5/1. It is rational."},
 IB21:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 21A2024, Part A · DOK 3", stem:`<p>An architect is considering a tower height of √200 meters. Is √200 rational or irrational?</p>`,
  type:"mc", opts:[["r","Rational","Did not check for a perfect square"],["i","Irrational",""]], ans:"i",
  why:"√200 = √(100 · 2) = 10√2. Since 200 is not a perfect square, √200 ≈ 14.142... never ends or repeats. It is irrational."},
 IB28:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 28A2024 · DOK 1", stem:`<p>A rectangle has side lengths of (x + 6) and (2x + 3). Write the area in standard form <span class="math">ax<sup>2</sup> + bx + c</span>. Enter a, b, and c.</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["a",2,0.001],["b",15,0.001],["c",18,0.001]], tagFor:(v,i) => i===1 ? "Did not combine the middle terms (3x + 12x)" : "Multiplying binomials error",
  why:"(x + 6)(2x + 3) = 2x<sup>2</sup> + 3x + 12x + 18 = 2x<sup>2</sup> + 15x + 18."},
 IB29C:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 29A2024, Part C · DOK 3", stem:`<p>The yogurt shop's poster must be a rectangle whose length is 2 inches more than twice the width. The shop changes the poster area to 144 square inches. Find the new dimensions.</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["Width (in)",8,0.001],["Length (in)",18,0.001]], tagFor:v => v===-9 ? "Kept the negative solution for a length" : "Quadratic setup or factoring error",
  why:"w(2w + 2) = 144 → 2w<sup>2</sup> + 2w − 144 = 0 → w<sup>2</sup> + w − 72 = 0 → (w + 9)(w − 8) = 0. w = 8 (reject −9). Length = 2(8) + 2 = 18. Check: 8 × 18 = 144 ✓."},
 IB31:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 31A2024 · DOK 3", stem:`<p>An Olympic pool is 164 ft by 82 ft. A concrete walkway of uniform width will go around it, and there is enough concrete for 4192 ft<sup>2</sup>. How wide can the walkway be?</p>`,
  type:"num", fields:[["Width (ft)",8,0.001]], tagFor:()=>"Quadratic setup error (walkway adds 2w to each dimension)",
  why:"Let w = walkway width. Outer rectangle: (164 + 2w)(82 + 2w). Walkway area = outer − pool: (164 + 2w)(82 + 2w) − 164 · 82 = 4192 → 4w<sup>2</sup> + 492w = 4192 → w<sup>2</sup> + 123w − 1048 = 0 → (w − 8)(w + 131) = 0. w = 8 ft."},
 IB40:{src:"GaDOE Item Bank 40A2024 · DOK 1", stem:`<p>Select the <b>three</b> contexts that could be represented by an exponential function.</p>`,
  type:"multi", opts:[["1","A coin collection appreciates at a rate of 17% per year"],["2","A music service has a fixed monthly cost and charges $0.20 for each downloaded song"],["3","A car depreciates at a rate of 2.5% per year"],["4","Money invested in a savings account grows at an annual rate of 3.4%"],["5","Snow was melting at a rate of 2.5 inches per hour"]], ans:["1","3","4"],
  wrongTags:{"1":"Missed a percent-rate (exponential) situation","2":"Called a constant-amount (linear) situation exponential","3":"Missed a percent-rate (exponential) situation","4":"Missed a percent-rate (exponential) situation","5":"Called a constant-amount (linear) situation exponential"},
